# question: What is the distinct set of measurements a device can produce?
# rationale: Walks each device's technical pathway (device -> functional unit
#   -> sensor -> signal -> metric) to list the distinct measurements it can
#   produce, grouped by device class.
#
# Purely technical: walks the device's measurement pathway as annotated in
# kg_generated.ttl (Device -> FunctionalUnit -> Sensor -> Signal ->
# SignalAnalysis -> Metric), grouped by the device's generic class
# (e.g. device:MechanicalVentilator), not by manufacturer/model -- that
# finer distinction is CQ7's question, not this one.
#
# The (analyzedBy/producesSignal)* hop covers derived/intermediate signals
# (e.g. a computed lead feeding a further analysis step) before the
# terminal analyzedBy/producesMetric hop. Since the derivation graphs
# (2026-11-24) this hop is load-bearing: every ECG-derived alarm (heart
# rate, and respiration rate from the ECG electrodes) runs electrode ->
# raw signal -> lead derivation -> lead -> analysis -> metric.
#
# Asserted only -- no inference.ttl predicate is involved, so this does not
# require the OWL-RL closure. Device classes whose only archetypes are
# connection/system-fault alarms have no measurement pathway at all and are
# correctly absent from the results, not a query defect (at p75:
# CardiacMonitor, Dialysator and Thermoregulator, e.g. "EDWARDS -
# Verbinding verbroken").
#
# The answer is bounded by the annotated alarms: a measurement a device
# never alarmed on in the corpus is not listed. Phase/aggregation variants
# (e.g. ArterialBloodPressure and ArterialBloodPressure_Mean,
# AirwayPressure_Peak and AirwayPressure_EndExpiratory) count as distinct
# measurements, as each is a distinct displayed value.

# 2026-11-24: metric hops added (build_framework.py derivation_graph()
# writes out derived metrics: cardiac output -> cardiac index). Every
# metric on the pathway counts as measured by the device, intermediate
# ones included, so no "own metric" filter here.

PREFIX mda: <https://w3id.org/mda/ontology#>
PREFIX skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#>

SELECT ?deviceClass (GROUP_CONCAT(DISTINCT ?metricNotation; separator=" | ") AS ?measurements)
       (COUNT(DISTINCT ?metricConcept) AS ?distinctCount) WHERE {
  ?a a mda:AlarmType ;
     mda:hasMessage/mda:triggeredBy ?deviceNode .
  ?deviceNode a ?deviceClass .
  ?deviceNode mda:hasFunctionalUnit/mda:hasSensor/mda:sensorProducesSignal/(mda:analyzedBy/(mda:producesSignal|mda:producesMetric))*/mda:analyzedBy/mda:producesMetric/a ?metricConcept .
  ?metricConcept skos:notation ?metricNotation .
}
GROUP BY ?deviceClass
ORDER BY ?deviceClass
